[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Mahendra","family":"Dwifebri","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"263","reference":[{"key":"ref10","article-title":"Fast and Accurate Sentiment Classification Using an Enhanced Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Model","author":"narayanan","year":"2013","journal-title":"Internation Coference on Intelligent Data Engineering and Automated Learning"},{"key":"ref11","author":"yenter","year":"2017","journal-title":"Deep CNN-LSTM with Combined Kernels from Multiple Branches for IMDb Review Sentiment Analysis"},{"key":"ref12","author":"tarimer","year":"2019","journal-title":"Sentiment Analysis on IMDB Movie Comments and Twitter Data by Machine Learning and Vector Space Techniques"},{"key":"ref13","author":"purnomoputra","year":"2019","journal-title":"Sentiment Analysis of Movie Reviews using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Method with Gini Index Feature Selection"},{"key":"ref14","author":"tripathi","year":"2020","journal-title":"Analyzing Sentiment using IMDb Dataset"},{"key":"ref15","author":"rahul shah","year":"2021","journal-title":"Movie Stats Sentiment Analysis of IMDB Reviews and Tweets of a Movie Using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Classifier"},{"key":"ref4","article-title":"Sentiment Analysis of Review Datasets using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes and K-NN Classifier","author":"dey","year":"2016","journal-title":"arXiv Cornell University Computer Science Information Retrieval"},{"key":"ref3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/ACCESS.2019.2909919"},{"key":"ref6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.22364\/bjmc.2017.5.4.06"},{"key":"ref5","article-title":"On the Feature Selection and Classification Based on Information Gain for Document Sentiment Analysis","author":"indah pratiwi","year":"2018","journal-title":"Applied Computational Intelligence and Soft Computing 2018"},{"key":"ref8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.5120\/ijca2017916005"},{"key":"ref7","article-title":"Sentiment Analysis on Twitter Posts : An analysis of Positive or Negative Opinion on Gojek","author":"pertiwi","year":"2017","journal-title":"Proc of 2017 4th Int Conf on Information Tech Computer and Electrical Engineering (ICITACEE)"},{"key":"ref2","article-title":"Sentiment Analysis on IMDb Movie Reviews Using Hybrid Feature Extraction Method","author":"keerthi kumar","year":"2018","journal-title":"International Journal of Interactive Multimedia and Artificial Intelligence"},{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-319-96136-1_15"},{"key":"ref9","first-page":"54","article-title":"Sentimental Analysis of Tweets Using Na&#x00EF;ve Bayes Algorithm","volume":"35","author":"vadivukarassi","year":"2017","journal-title":"World Applied Sciences Journal"}],"event":{"name":"2021 3rd International Conference on Electronics Representation and Algorithm (ICERA)","location":"Yogyakarta, Indonesia","start":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]},"end":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,30]]}},"container-title":["2021 3rd International Conference on Electronics Representation and Algorithm (ICERA)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx7\/9538521\/9538631\/09538763.pdf?arnumber=9538763","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,10]],"date-time":"2022-05-10T15:46:10Z","timestamp":1652197570000},"score":37.49706,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/9538763\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]},"references-count":15,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icera53111.2021.9538763","published":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,29]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,31]],"date-time":"2025-12-31T02:49:04Z","timestamp":1767149344647,"version":"3.48.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Politeknik Negeri Batam","issue":"6","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]],"date-time":"2025-12-06T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1764979200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-sa\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["JAIC"],"abstract":"<jats:p>This study aims to classify user opinions on IMDb movie reviews using the Multinomial Na\u00efve Bayes algorithm. The dataset consists of 50,000 reviews, evenly distributed between 25,000 positive and 25,000 negative reviews. The preprocessing stage includes cleaning, case folding, stopword removal, tokenization, and lemmatization using the NLTK library. Text features are represented through the TF-IDF method to capture the significance of each word in the documents. The Multinomial Na\u00efve Bayes model was trained using the hold-out validation technique with an 80:20 split for training and testing data. Hyperparameter tuning of \u03b1 (Laplace smoothing) was conducted to enhance model stability and accuracy. The model\u2019s performance was evaluated using accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score metrics, supported by a confusion matrix visualization. The results show that the model achieved an accuracy of 87%, with precision of 87.9%, recall of 85.4%, and an F1-score of 86.6%. In comparison, Logistic Regression as a baseline algorithm achieved an accuracy of 91%. Nevertheless, the Na\u00efve Bayes algorithm remains competitive and computationally efficient for large-scale text data, making it highly relevant for sentiment analysis of movie reviews.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.30871\/jaic.v9i6.9831","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,31]],"date-time":"2025-12-31T02:36:41Z","timestamp":1767148601000},"page":"3168-3176","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Opinion Classification on IMDb Reviews Using Na\u00efve Bayes Algorithm"],"prefix":"10.30871","volume":"9","author":[{"given":"Amiliya","family":"Putri","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Khothibul","family":"Umam","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hery","family":"Mustofa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"12321","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]]},"container-title":["Journal of Applied Informatics and Computing"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.polibatam.ac.id\/index.php\/JAIC\/article\/download\/9831\/3178","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.polibatam.ac.id\/index.php\/JAIC\/article\/download\/9831\/3178","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,31]],"date-time":"2025-12-31T02:39:09Z","timestamp":1767148749000},"score":37.48872,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.polibatam.ac.id\/index.php\/JAIC\/article\/view\/9831"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"6","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,12]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.30871\/jaic.v9i6.9831","ISSN":["2548-6861"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2548-6861","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,6]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T09:31:43Z","timestamp":1772271103375,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011\/supp-1","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,30]],"date-time":"2024-04-30T04:34:13Z","timestamp":1714451653000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Supplemental Information 1: The YELP-5 dataset is a sentiment classification task dataset used for sentiment analysis. It comprises user reviews sourced from the Yelp website"],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,30]],"date-time":"2024-04-30T04:34:19Z","